{"id":"01a047e0-b3f4-7ec9-b215-8a5567c8c4de","issue_id":"project-LICHEN-worker6-l1qw.9.14.9.2","event_type":"closed","actor":"Mark Atwood","old_value":"","new_value":"Rust Confessions implementation complete, committed 483d6e8afe (lib.rs staged HEAD+my-hunks to avoid the concurrent worker's in-flight presence WIP). Completed the dead session's partial module: fixed compile errors (undeclared payload_had_anonymous, missing helpers), rewrote to_senml for canonical byte-parity, added ConfessionStore mirroring the Python oracle (rate limits 1/30s + 12/h on monotonic uptime with Retry-After and vector reasons 30s_limit / hourly_limit_exceeded, FIFO eviction no back-pressure, TTL clamp 12h/48h, CSPRNG 6-hex ids with bounded retries, listing sorted newest-first per vector, RAM-only clear(), sender stored only when claimed bn == authenticated IID, Error::Config for zero storage per h443 convention). tests/confessions_vectors.rs drives all 17 vectors: the one byte-pinned hex (anonymous_confession_default, repaired by 2yps) decodes and re-encodes byte-exact; store sequences (rate 12th/13th, 30s window, FIFO 600B, BR budget, reboot warm/crash, size 768/769, ttl_expiry, get metadata, no-log) assert against vector expectations. Results: confessions_vectors 17/17, lichen-client --lib 130/130, checkin_rollcall_vectors 13/13, deaddrop_vectors 27/27; Python oracle test_confessions_resource.py 56/56; cargo fmt + clippy clean for the module. Note: listing is ts-descending (vector-pinned) which matches the Python oracle for chronological inserts; wire bytes only pinned for the default vector.","created_at":"2026-08-28T10:18:23.60497Z"}
